of churn.\n","- Customers without technical support or online security services are more likely to churn.\n","\n","These insights can help the telecom company develop targeted customer retention strategies, such as promoting long-term contracts, improving service quality, and offering bundled support services."],"metadata":{"id":"C8NGiI9oO0Rc"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["shap.summary_plot(shap_values, X_test, plot_type=\"bar\")"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":957},"id":"9rvhJPxuH8in","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1783185360530,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":813,"user":{"displayName":"Yash","userId":"08944414725317633232"}},"outputId":"54ed49b2-94bc-45b2-8813-a2c8c09892d1"},"execution_count":58,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 800x950 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### Interpretation\n","\n","The SHAP Feature Importance Bar Plot ranks the features according to their average contribution toward model predictions.\n","\n","Among all variables, **Contract_Month-to-month** has the highest impact on customer churn prediction, followed by **tenure**, **Fiber Optic Internet Service**, **Monthly Charges**, **Technical Support**, and **Online Security**.\n","\n","Unlike the SHAP Summary Plot, this visualization focuses only on the magnitude of feature importance and does not indicate whether the impact is positive or negative.\n","\n","This ranking helps identify the most influential business factors that should be prioritized in customer retention strategies."],"metadata":{"id":"4TmETpp3QgbL"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["shap.plots.waterfall(explainer(X_test.iloc[[0]])[0])"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":512},"id":"HhnneLSHH8ay","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1783185368805,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":567,"user":{"displayName":"Yash","userId":"08944414725317633232"}},"outputId":"12c1b511-d035-4267-8c62-2de9bf2d00e0"},"execution_count":59,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 800x650 with 3 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### Interpretation\n","\n","The SHAP Waterfall Plot explains the prediction for an individual customer.\n","\n","Starting from the model's baseline prediction, each feature either increases or decreases the customer's probability of churning.\n","\n","Positive SHAP values push the prediction toward churn, while negative SHAP values reduce the likelihood of churn.\n","\n","For this customer, features such as **Month-to-Month Contract**, **High Monthly Charges**, and **Short Tenure** contribute positively toward churn, whereas features like **Longer Tenure**, **Technical Support**, or **Online Security** may reduce the churn probability.\n","\n","This visualization provides local interpretability by explaining why the model made a particular prediction for one customer."],"metadata":{"id":"kYUjkpKlQj66"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["shap.dependence_plot(\"tenure\", shap_values, X_test)"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":476},"id":"O-SJctX_H8N_","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1783185374164,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":561,"user":{"displayName":"Yash","userId":"08944414725317633232"}},"outputId":"a64851e0-5616-42fc-f25c-5bf90c7d4e6a"},"execution_count":60,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 750x500 with 2 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### Interpretation\n","\n","The SHAP Dependence Plot illustrates the relationship between the **tenure** feature and its impact on churn prediction.\n","\n","Customers with lower tenure generally have positive SHAP values, indicating a higher likelihood of churn.\n","\n","As tenure increases, SHAP values gradually decrease, suggesting that long-term customers are less likely to leave the company.\n","\n","This trend indicates that customer loyalty strengthens over time, highlighting the importance of retention programs during the initial months of a customer's subscription."],"metadata":{"id":"tkjs8mNSQxcG"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#Bussiness Insights"],"metadata":{"id":"iHBWEfWPQ18k"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Business Recommendations\n","\n","Based on the SHAP analysis, the following recommendations can help reduce customer churn:\n","\n","- Encourage customers to switch from month-to-month contracts to long-term contracts by offering discounts and loyalty incentives.\n","- Implement customer engagement programs for new customers during the first few months to improve retention.\n","- Review pricing strategies for customers with high monthly charges and offer personalized plans where appropriate.\n","- Improve the quality of Fiber Optic Internet Service and address customer complaints proactively.\n","- Promote value-added services such as Technical Support and Online Security through bundled offers to enhance customer satisfaction."],"metadata":{"id":"ukOKWNxJQ87S"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#Conclusion"],"metadata":{"id":"wdlvDCQvRUAw"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Conclusion\n","\n","In this project, an end-to-end Customer Churn Prediction model was developed using supervised machine learning techniques. The dataset was preprocessed through data cleaning, feature engineering, and exploratory data analysis to identify the major factors influencing customer churn.\n","\n","Multiple machine learning algorithms were trained and evaluated, including Logistic Regression, Decision Tree, Random Forest, AdaBoost, and XGBoost. Among these models, XGBoost achieved the best performance after hyperparameter tuning using GridSearchCV, with an accuracy of approximately **82.5%**.\n","\n","The model's performance was further evaluated using the Confusion Matrix and Classification Report, providing insights into precision, recall, and F1-score. These metrics demonstrated the model's effectiveness in identifying customers who are likely to churn.\n","\n","To improve model interpretability, SHAP (SHapley Additive exPlanations) was used to explain the predictions. SHAP analysis revealed that **Month-to-Month Contract**, **Customer Tenure**, **Fiber Optic Internet Service**, **Monthly Charges**, **Technical Support**, and **Online Security** were the most influential factors affecting customer churn.\n","\n","Based on these findings, the telecom company can implement targeted retention strategies such as promoting long-term contracts, improving customer support services, offering competitive pricing plans, and focusing on customers with shorter tenure. Such data-driven decisions can help reduce customer churn, improve customer satisfaction, and increase long-term business profitability."],"metadata":{"id":"mci0FIGqRWgR"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["model.save_model(\"churn_model.json\")"],"metadata":{"id":"tcty_EIXljA0","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1783193028040,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":41,"user":{"displayName":"Yash","userId":"08944414725317633232"}}},"execution_count":63,"outputs":[]}]}